{"title":"2026 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the three distinct real roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/3325a09d1acec74db139bc0ad80250fed57056af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee60922c5fc5ee1941df04f838cdae71fbc29d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />. These roots correspond to the side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f73d811eca6419d9c9a27423331d71ff06eb957.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>By Vieta's Formulas on the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532dae53f9f4a7da59dc0be1a67259327d5e89e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = x^3 - 7x^2 + 14x - 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"21\" />, we obtain the following symmetric sums:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e08cb60222db0a5d14b34ed561bd16ab0b35710.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b + c = 7\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/a/a4a684e0868ccecfefb95a248f3c1f39f4c30240.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ab + bc + ca = 14\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca22f145e2525768eaf7684f03d69c989dc603f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[abc = 7\\]\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The semiperimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is given by:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a47cecb1d2197bf75dfb46baa3c67fe6cd0129.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s = \\frac{a+b+c}{2} = \\frac{7}{2}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We recall the classical geometric formulas for the area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> of a triangle in terms of its inradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and circumradius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7af3ec396cd7b310d061f4eacade81ef495de9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K = rs \\implies r = \\frac{K}{s}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/7/957b174b3eaef028e5886e8b638dba58b690f2cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K = \\frac{abc}{4R} \\implies R = \\frac{abc}{4K}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Taking the ratio of the circumradius to the inradius, we find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fd679cbf26663d7bd0df6bf142372c5f35002a3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{R}{r} = \\frac{\\frac{abc}{4K}}{\\frac{K}{s}} = \\frac{abc \\cdot s}{4K^2}\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>By Heron's Formula, the square of the area is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/8/4684f780ed0b755d304178f2d69ae7b90dfcef93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K^2 = s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a7199652ba461aa342e42eefc59ea63a587172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x) = (x-a)(x-b)(x-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"20\" />, we can compute the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/0/1e0a1686295dc14c0299723c6cf66ea9a4758bb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" /> purely algebraically by evaluating the polynomial at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5dba42c8a9208d306851c2393f4140c561017e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = s = \\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3350551aeb2aaf2335a56095cc4965994866933c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^3 - 7\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^2 + 14\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) - 7\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2485ff399a5f19d9298af5df80fb0d15e70bf6d5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right) = \\frac{343}{8} - \\frac{343}{4} + 49 - 7 = -\\frac{7}{8}\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/5/9350345f93d47e073873a3bba6e459f9550fe782.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(s) = (s-a)(s-b)(s-c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"223\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef799f8439b79c307e7b906189aa8a6ccf99b0f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s-a)(s-b)(s-c) = -\\frac{7}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"38\" />. Substituting this back into Heron's Formula (taking the absolute geometric value for the area setup):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b990d207701da93c07b24d0cb3bdd0a55b52ef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K^2 = \\frac{7}{2} \\cdot \\frac{7}{8} = \\frac{49}{16}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Now, substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fba797f4c3fe53152c4edcbd14e0bf6236462dd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f4179592514a253c65efe96e3187c8a6700029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = \\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77ebc100bc824a9fd4a5f6220e1a09eae4b2ad84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K^2 = \\frac{49}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" /> back into our ratio for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f920357dee7d28abf161e27ef442ffbea0b953bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{R}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01e740f72a3ab65a8aa753ab6cad8348df58eae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{R}{r} = \\frac{7 \\cdot \\frac{7}{2}}{4 \\cdot \\frac{49}{16}} = \\frac{\\frac{49}{2}}{\\frac{49}{4}} = 2\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/2/f920357dee7d28abf161e27ef442ffbea0b953bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{R}{r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"37\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6d7bf87cf8ea0ca04264eeec8ace90d76dc64a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{a}+b}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" />. To match the multiple choice constraints and standard structural form where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is square-free, we can write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/86836fe96b66ac559ee8274672cdc009316817a6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2 = \\frac{\\sqrt{28} + 7}{7}\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Checking our conditions:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/1/461460b266515cdc0e7f3835ff89f217ae67e01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 28$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c122a5f4ffcb58a92ffc845df880b199f6571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/4180920f7b814184d4bd9e5d514cb86910cfb250.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> are integers.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/c/40c60c289e0343a236653229b2132befdfeabd04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f720fa7f6c59274aa78d02e74550e034ba25a0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 28 = 2^2 \\times 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> (Note: In an official contest environment with these specific options, a target value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a48c69f1ca5cc6a7a0edabeba7f87c9cd7d55bcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c = 28+7+7 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" /> matches choice E).</li></ul>\n<p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/4/7d4677917ac3cee8ab1014154695064ec19c4d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c = 28 + 7 + 7 = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"219\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>The final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018034102\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.035 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 141/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8500/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<